From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:25:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] context: keep up to 16 bitstream buffers in flight

The OUTPUT ring held 4 bitstream buffers, so at most three requests
were queued while the next picture was being filled, and the fourth
picture waited for the oldest one to be dequeued. The Apple Video
Decoder's kernel driver keeps up to 16 frames in flight in the
firmware's queue, one per frame-parameter slot, so a client that does
not sync every picture (ffmpeg, GStreamer, a browser decoding ahead)
left the decoder idle between pictures.

Make the ring 16 buffers deep. The queued masks are 32 bits wide, and
a decoder that keeps fewer frames in flight holds the extra requests in
its own queue as before. Each buffer is still created at the decoder's
sizeimage and grown on demand.

The failure-cleanup model's capture-queue case now cycles one ring of
synced surfaces twice instead of creating a surface per picture, so a
16-deep ring stays inside the model's 32 CAPTURE indices.
---
 src/v4l2_request.h      | 2 +-
 tests/failure-cleanup.c | 9 +++++++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/v4l2_request.h b/src/v4l2_request.h
index b14090b..a3d45d4 100644
--- a/src/v4l2_request.h
+++ b/src/v4l2_request.h
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ static inline uint64_t v4l2r_now_ns(void)
 #define V4L2R_MAX_PIXELFORMATS		16
 
 /* Number of OUTPUT (bitstream) buffers in the per-context circular queue. */
-#define V4L2R_OUTPUT_BUFFERS		4
+#define V4L2R_OUTPUT_BUFFERS		16
 /* Largest CAPTURE buffer count we can track in the queued bitmask. With a
  * per-frame buffer pool the count reaches roughly the client's live surface
  * count plus the pipeline depth, so keep headroom up to the 64-bit bitmask. */
diff --git a/tests/failure-cleanup.c b/tests/failure-cleanup.c
index a4c92a3..f3a8711 100644
--- a/tests/failure-cleanup.c
+++ b/tests/failure-cleanup.c
@@ -865,9 +865,14 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
         armed = false; failed_surface(sid);
         if (!strcmp(test, "capture-queue")) {
             /* An idle request can be reinitialized. Exercise a full ring
-             * twice: without release the stranded OUTPUT slot times out. */
+             * twice: without release the stranded OUTPUT slot times out.
+             * Each picture is synced, so one ring of surfaces is cycled
+             * twice and the model's 32 CAPTURE indices are not outgrown. */
+            VASurfaceID ring[V4L2R_OUTPUT_BUFFERS];
+            for (unsigned int n = 0; n < V4L2R_OUTPUT_BUFFERS; n++)
+                ring[n] = surface();
             for (unsigned int n = 0; n < 2 * V4L2R_OUTPUT_BUFFERS; n++) {
-                VASurfaceID next = surface();
+                VASurfaceID next = ring[n % V4L2R_OUTPUT_BUFFERS];
                 assert(picture(id, next) == VA_STATUS_SUCCESS);
                 assert(table.vaSyncSurface(&va, next) == VA_STATUS_SUCCESS);
             }
